{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ruinable-cozey-caracal","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe close-reason and force plumbing is computed independently on each surface: the \"reason persists only on a REASON_REQUIRED class without force\" rule lives at `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:584`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:318`, and `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:357-362`; the `\"(no reason given)\"` placeholder at `transition.py:388`, `claim.py:38`, `_lib_writes.py:412`; one datum travels as `force_reason` → `force_close` → `force_close_reason` across three files. The CLI refuses an inadmissible reason while the library silently discards it, and MCP `transition_ticket` (`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:224-232`) does not expose `reason` at all — the strict-xfail row in `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:34-35,193` (bug `scratchy-leprous-galago`). Bug `defiant-orthoclase-buck` was the datum accepted under one name and never read.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_commands/transition_request.py` with a frozen `TransitionRequest(ticket_id, current, target, close_class, reason, force, caused_by, ref)` exposing `force_note`, `close_reason`, and `reason_refusal()`. All three surfaces construct it; `txn.transition_core` and `close_ticket` read the properties. MCP `transition_ticket` gains `reason` by constructing the same object, which flips the strict-xfail to a pass and forces its removal. Guard: the placeholder literal and the REASON_REQUIRED admission test appear only in `transition_request.py`.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_commands/transition_request.py` (new), `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_transition_request.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: each surface closing a REASON_REQUIRED class with a reason persists it. Edge: a reason on a non-reason class is refused identically on CLI, lib, and MCP (the parity oracle row). Pinning: `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`, `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py`, `tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py` pass unchanged except the removed xfail marker.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The `write_parity_contract.py` reason row passes on all three adapters with its strict-xfail removed; checked by `pytest tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`.\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"no reason given\" src/rebar` returns one file; checked by the grep and the guard test.\n- [ ] Persisted `force_close_reason` and `close_reason` events are byte-identical to today for the pinning suites; checked by those suites passing unchanged.\n","id":"825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"TransitionRequest value object: one close-reason/force rule across CLI, library and MCP"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787352169660438001,"uuid":"3aa3cd31-bb7e-4538-97ff-844ec2ae6088"}